      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine reconciliation by reused Codex non-author c05_253_255_reconcile. Original producers were primary Codex, Tibetan-first with prior preparation, and reused peer c05_262_264_english, English-first. This is not human editorial acceptance. The two source gsum numerals own the first and third English three, for beings and objects; three karmas is an English contextual reprise. Can/with is attributive d6 and cig car du/all together is a complete simultaneous-viewing phrase. Skye ba/start to be and the red-hot compound retain their tighter attested lexical boundaries. Yod owns the initial There is; Suppose there is is supplied framing. Each of the two complete lcags sngags/mantra of steel names has unique lcags/steel and sngags/mantra members; the third abbreviated title keeps sngags/mantra only. The single byas pa owns the second provides, for the contributing factor. Three active-agentive relations have no separate English words. Gzhan/other and zhig/some remain separate lexical/particle atoms. Four reg bya occurrences own the four sensations in order; myong owns undergo, myong ba feels, and later myong feel. The final myong has no separately repeated verb under the coordinated no-other-sensation object and is an explicit elliptical null, not loss of its experiential meaning. The three negations retain distinct scopes. Later time clauses and supplied participants/auxiliaries remain unwrapped. No source or glossary is changed."
